#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:5
msgid "ギブス自由エネルギー"
msgstr "Gibbs Free Energy"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:10
msgid "標準反応ギブスエネルギー"
msgstr "Standard Reaction Gibbs Energy"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:12
msgid ""
"\\Delta_r G^o = \\Delta_r H^o - T \\Delta_r S^o\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta_r G^o = \\Delta_r H^o - T \\Delta_r S^o\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:18
msgid "標準生成ギブスエネルギー"
msgstr "Standard Gibbs Energy of Formation"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:20
msgid ""
"化合物1 molが、\\ :ref:`基準状態<reference_state>`\\ "
"にある構成元素から生成する反応の標準反応ギブスエネルギーを、 標準生成ギブスエネルギー :math:`\\Delta_f G^o` "
"と呼ぶ。標準生成エンタルピーと同じく基準状態の元素では0で、 任意の反応の標準反応ギブスエネルギーは"
msgstr ""
"The standard reaction Gibbs energy for forming 1 mol of a compound from "
"its constituent elements in their \\ :ref:`reference states "
"<reference_state>`\\  is called the standard Gibbs energy of formation, "
":math:`\\Delta_f G^o`. As with the standard enthalpy of formation, it is "
"zero for an element in its reference state, and the standard reaction "
"Gibbs energy of any reaction is"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:24
msgid "\\Delta_r G^o=\\sum_i\\nu_i\\Delta_f G_i^o"
msgstr "\\Delta_r G^o=\\sum_i\\nu_i\\Delta_f G_i^o"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:29
msgid ""
"で求まる。生成反応に前の節の式を当てはめると :math:`\\Delta_f G^o=\\Delta_f H^o-T\\Delta_f S^o`"
" で、 :math:`\\Delta_f S^o` は生成反応の標準反応エントロピーである。元素の標準エントロピーは0でないので、 "
":math:`\\Delta_f S^o` には元素の項が残る。"
msgstr ""
"Applying the equation of the previous section to the formation reaction "
"gives :math:`\\Delta_f G^o=\\Delta_f H^o-T\\Delta_f S^o`, where "
":math:`\\Delta_f S^o` is the standard reaction entropy of the formation "
"reaction. Because the standard entropies of the elements are not zero, "
":math:`\\Delta_f S^o` retains the terms for the elements."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:38
msgid "化学ポテンシャル"
msgstr "Chemical Potential"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:40
msgid ""
"物質が相の間を移るか、反応がどちらへ進むかは、成分ごとの化学ポテンシャルで決まる。 温度 :math:`T`、圧力 :math:`p` と、各成分"
" :math:`i` の物質量 :math:`n_i` を変数として ギブス自由エネルギー "
":math:`G(T,p,n_1,\\ldots,n_k)` をみると、その微小変化は"
msgstr ""
"The chemical potential of each component determines whether it transfers "
"between phases and in which direction a reaction proceeds. Taking "
"temperature :math:`T`, pressure :math:`p`, and, for each component "
":math:`i`, its amount of substance :math:`n_i` as variables, we can write"
" the differential of the Gibbs free energy :math:`G(T,p,n_1,\\ldots,n_k)`"
" as"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:44
msgid "dG=-S\\,dT+V\\,dp+\\sum_i\\mu_i\\,dn_i"
msgstr "dG=-S\\,dT+V\\,dp+\\sum_i\\mu_i\\,dn_i"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:49
msgid "と書ける [ThermoCallen1985]_。:math:`S` はエントロピー、:math:`V` は体積である。係数"
msgstr ""
"This is the form given in [ThermoCallen1985]_. Here :math:`S` is the "
"entropy and :math:`V` is the volume. The coefficient"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:51
msgid ""
"\\mu_i=\\left(\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial n_i}\\right)_{T,p,n_{j\\neq "
"i}}"
msgstr ""
"\\mu_i=\\left(\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial n_i}\\right)_{T,p,n_{j\\neq "
"i}}"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:56
msgid ""
"を成分 :math:`i` の **化学ポテンシャル** と呼ぶ。温度・圧力とほかの成分の量を固定して、 成分 :math:`i` "
"を少し加えたときの :math:`G` の増え方である。単位はJ/molである。"
msgstr ""
"for component :math:`i` is called its **chemical potential**. When a "
"small amount of component :math:`i` is added at fixed temperature and "
"pressure and with the amounts of the other components held fixed, this "
"coefficient gives the rate of change of :math:`G`. Its unit is J/mol."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:59
msgid ""
"**ギブス自由エネルギーとの関係。** 温度と圧力を固定して系の全成分を :math:`\\lambda` 倍すると、 :math:`G` も "
":math:`\\lambda` 倍になる。:math:`G(T,p,\\lambda n_1,\\ldots,\\lambda "
"n_k)=\\lambda G(T,p,n_1,\\ldots,n_k)` の両辺を :math:`\\lambda` で微分して "
":math:`\\lambda=1` とおくと、:eq:`thermo-chemical-potential`\\ から"
msgstr ""
"**Relation to Gibbs free energy.** At fixed temperature and pressure, "
"multiplying the amounts of all components by :math:`\\lambda` also "
"multiplies :math:`G` by :math:`\\lambda`. Differentiating both sides of "
":math:`G(T,p,\\lambda n_1,\\ldots,\\lambda n_k)=\\lambda "
"G(T,p,n_1,\\ldots,n_k)` with respect to :math:`\\lambda` and setting "
":math:`\\lambda=1` gives, by Equation :eq:`thermo-chemical-potential`\\ ,"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:63
msgid "G=\\sum_i n_i\\mu_i"
msgstr "G=\\sum_i n_i\\mu_i"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:68
msgid ""
"を得る。純物質では :math:`\\mu=G/n` で、化学ポテンシャルは1 molあたりのギブス自由エネルギーに等しい。 "
"**反応ギブスエネルギー。** 反応 :math:`\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mathrm A_i=0`\\ （:math:`\\nu_i` "
"は生成物で正、反応物で負の 化学量論係数）の進み具合を反応進行度 :math:`\\xi`\\ （単位はmol）で表すと、反応が "
":math:`d\\xi` だけ進むとき 各成分の物質量は :math:`dn_i=\\nu_i\\,d\\xi` だけ変わる。これを\\ :eq"
":`thermo-gibbs-differential`\\ に入れると、 温度と圧力が一定のもとで"
msgstr ""
"For a pure substance, :math:`\\mu=G/n`, so the chemical potential equals "
"the Gibbs free energy per mole. **Reaction Gibbs energy.** For a reaction"
" :math:`\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mathrm A_i=0`\\  (where :math:`\\nu_i` is the "
"stoichiometric coefficient, positive for products and negative for "
"reactants), let the extent of reaction :math:`\\xi`\\  (in mol) describe "
"how far the reaction has proceeded. When the reaction advances by "
":math:`d\\xi`, the amount of substance of each component changes by "
":math:`dn_i=\\nu_i\\,d\\xi`. Substituting this into Equation \\ :eq"
":`thermo-gibbs-differential`\\  at fixed temperature and pressure gives"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:74
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\Delta_r G\\equiv\\left(\\frac{\\partial "
"G}{\\partial\\xi}\\right)_{T,p}=\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mu_i"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta_r G\\equiv\\left(\\frac{\\partial "
"G}{\\partial\\xi}\\right)_{T,p}=\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mu_i"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:79
msgid ""
"を得る。:math:`\\Delta_r G` は、その時点の組成で反応を微小に進めたときの :math:`G` の変化率である。 "
"反応が有限量進むと組成が変わり、各 :math:`\\mu_i` も変わるので、:math:`G` の有限の変化は :eq:`thermo-"
"reaction-gibbs`\\ を :math:`\\xi` について積分したものになる。 各成分が\\ "
":ref:`標準状態<standard_state>`\\ にあるときの\\ :eq:`thermo-reaction-gibbs`\\ の値が、"
" この記事の最初の節の標準反応ギブスエネルギー :math:`\\Delta_r G^o=\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mu_i^o` である。"
msgstr ""
"At the current composition, :math:`\\Delta_r G` is the rate of change of "
":math:`G` for an infinitesimal advance of the reaction. Over a finite "
"advance, the composition changes and so does each :math:`\\mu_i`. The "
"finite change in :math:`G` is therefore the integral of Equation :eq"
":`thermo-reaction-gibbs`\\  with respect to :math:`\\xi`. When each "
"component is in its \\ :ref:`standard state <standard_state>`\\ , "
"Equation \\ :eq:`thermo-reaction-gibbs`\\  gives the standard reaction "
"Gibbs energy in the first section of this article, :math:`\\Delta_r "
"G^o=\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mu_i^o`."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:85
msgid ""
"**相平衡の条件。** 同じ温度・圧力の2つの相 :math:`\\alpha`、:math:`\\beta` の間で、成分 :math:`i` "
"を :math:`dn` だけ :math:`\\alpha` から :math:`\\beta` へ移すと、:eq:`thermo-gibbs-"
"differential`\\ から"
msgstr ""
"**Condition for phase equilibrium.** Consider two phases, :math:`\\alpha`"
" and :math:`\\beta`, at the same temperature and pressure. If component "
":math:`i` is transferred in an amount :math:`dn` from :math:`\\alpha` to "
":math:`\\beta`, Equation :eq:`thermo-gibbs-differential`\\  gives"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:88
msgid "dG=\\left(\\mu_i^\\beta-\\mu_i^\\alpha\\right)dn"
msgstr "dG=\\left(\\mu_i^\\beta-\\mu_i^\\alpha\\right)dn"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:93
msgid ""
"となる。温度と圧力が一定のとき、自発的な変化は :math:`G` を下げる向きに進むので、 "
"成分は化学ポテンシャルの高い相から低い相へ移る。平衡では :math:`dn` の正負どちらに対しても :math:`dG=0` なので、"
msgstr ""
"At fixed temperature and pressure, spontaneous changes lower :math:`G`, "
"so the component moves from the phase with higher chemical potential to "
"the phase with lower chemical potential. At equilibrium, for either sign "
"of :math:`dn` we have :math:`dG=0`, so"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:97
msgid "\\mu_i^\\alpha=\\mu_i^\\beta"
msgstr "\\mu_i^\\alpha=\\mu_i^\\beta"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:102
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"が成り立つ。反応についても同じ考え方で、平衡では :math:`\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mu_i=0` になる。 "
"例えば酸素分子と酸素原子の平衡 :math:`\\mathrm O_2\\rightleftharpoons2\\mathrm O` からは "
":math:`\\mu_{\\mathrm O}=\\mu_{\\mathrm O_2}/2` が従う。"
msgstr ""
"The same reasoning applies to reactions. At equilibrium, "
":math:`\\sum_i\\nu_i\\mu_i=0`. For example, the equilibrium between "
"molecular and atomic oxygen, :math:`\\mathrm "
"O_2\\rightleftharpoons2\\mathrm O`, implies :math:`\\mu_{\\mathrm "
"O}=\\mu_{\\mathrm O_2}/2`."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:106
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**理想気体の圧力依存性。** :eq:`thermo-gibbs-differential`\\ で :math:`G` "
"の2階微分の順序を入れ替えると :math:`(\\partial\\mu_i/\\partial p)_{T,n}=(\\partial "
"V/\\partial n_i)_{T,p}` で、純物質の右辺は1 molあたりの体積 :math:`V_{\\rm m}` "
"である。理想気体では :math:`V_{\\rm m}=RT/p`\\ （:math:`R` は気体定数）なので、 標準圧力 "
":math:`p^o=1\\,\\mathrm{bar}` から :math:`p` まで積分すると"
msgstr ""
"**Pressure dependence for an ideal gas.** Using Equation :eq:`thermo-"
"gibbs-differential`\\ , we reverse the order of differentiation in the "
"mixed second derivative of :math:`G` and obtain "
":math:`(\\partial\\mu_i/\\partial p)_{T,n}=(\\partial V/\\partial "
"n_i)_{T,p}`. For a pure substance, the right-hand side is the volume per "
"mole, :math:`V_{\\rm m}`. For an ideal gas, :math:`V_{\\rm m}=RT/p`\\  "
"(where :math:`R` is the gas constant). Integrating from the standard "
"pressure :math:`p^o=1\\,\\mathrm{bar}` to :math:`p` therefore gives"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:111
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mu(T,p)=\\mu^o(T)+RT\\ln\\frac{p}{p^o}"
msgstr "\\mu(T,p)=\\mu^o(T)+RT\\ln\\frac{p}{p^o}"

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:116
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`\\mu^o(T)` は温度 :math:`T` の標準状態での値である。理想気体の混合物では、 :math:`p` "
"を成分の分圧に置き換える。"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`\\mu^o(T)` is the value in the standard state at temperature "
":math:`T`. For a mixture of ideal gases, replace :math:`p` with the "
"partial pressure of the component."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:119
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**1粒子あたりの値。** 第一原理計算や統計力学では、化学ポテンシャルを1粒子（1原子や1分子） あたりのエネルギーで表すことが多い。1 "
"molあたりの値をアボガドロ定数 :math:`N_{\\rm A}` で割ると 1粒子あたりの値になり、:math:`R/N_{\\rm "
"A}=k_{\\rm B}`\\ （ボルツマン定数）なので、 :eq:`thermo-ideal-gas-mu`\\ の第2項は "
":math:`k_{\\rm B}T\\ln(p/p^o)` になる。 1 eV/粒子は96.485 "
"kJ/molにあたる。分圧を10倍にすると化学ポテンシャルは :math:`k_{\\rm B}T\\ln10` だけ上がり、 300 "
"Kで0.0595 eV（5.74 kJ/mol）、1100 °C（1373 K）で0.272 eVである。 "
"高温の気相と原子をやりとりする表面では、分圧を1けた変えるだけで0.1 eVを超える差が生じる。"
msgstr ""
"**Value per particle.** In first-principles calculations and statistical "
"mechanics, the chemical potential is often expressed as an energy per "
"particle (an atom or a molecule). Dividing the value per mole by the "
"Avogadro constant :math:`N_{\\rm A}` gives the value per particle. Since "
":math:`R/N_{\\rm A}=k_{\\rm B}`\\  (the Boltzmann constant), the second "
"term in Equation :eq:`thermo-ideal-gas-mu`\\  becomes :math:`k_{\\rm "
"B}T\\ln(p/p^o)`. An energy of 1 eV per particle corresponds to 96.485 "
"kJ/mol. Increasing the partial pressure by a factor of 10 raises the "
"chemical potential by :math:`k_{\\rm B}T\\ln10`. The increase is 0.0595 "
"eV (5.74 kJ/mol) at 300 K and 0.272 eV at 1100 °C (1373 K). For a surface"
" exchanging atoms with a high-temperature gas phase, changing the partial"
" pressure by just one order of magnitude shifts the chemical potential by"
" more than 0.1 eV."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:127
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**固体の化学ポテンシャルと全エネルギー。** 単体の固体では、:eq:`thermo-gibbs-euler`\\ から "
":math:`\\mu=G/N=(E+pV-TS)/N`\\ （:math:`N` は原子数、:math:`E` は内部エネルギー）である。 1 "
"barでの1原子あたりの :math:`pV/N` は、1原子あたりの体積 :math:`V/N` を20 Å\\ :sup:`3`\\ としても"
" 約 :math:`1\\times10^{-5}` eVで、無視できる。絶対零度で零点振動も無視すると、:math:`\\mu` "
"は1原子あたりの全エネルギーで近似できる。 第一原理計算で原子の出入りを含むエネルギーを比べるとき、単体の固体や孤立分子の全エネルギーを "
"化学ポテンシャルの基準に使うのはこのためである。気相では、全エネルギーに 温度と分圧に依存する部分を加える（`GaN表面の相図 "
"<https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/gan_surface/phase_diagram.html>`__\\ の気相の化学ポテンシャル）。"
msgstr ""
"**Chemical potential and total energy of a solid.** For an elemental "
"solid, Equation :eq:`thermo-gibbs-euler`\\  gives :math:`\\mu=G/N=(E+pV-"
"TS)/N`\\  (where :math:`N` is the number of atoms and :math:`E` is the "
"internal energy). At 1 bar, the per-atom term :math:`pV/N` is only about "
":math:`1\\times10^{-5}` eV even for a volume per atom :math:`V/N` of 20 "
"Å\\ :sup:`3`\\ , and can be neglected. At absolute zero, if zero-point "
"vibration is also neglected, :math:`\\mu` can be approximated by the "
"total energy per atom. This is why first-principles calculations use the "
"total energy of an elemental solid or an isolated molecule as a reference"
" for the chemical potential when comparing energies that involve adding "
"or removing atoms. For the gas phase, add a contribution that depends on "
"temperature and partial pressure to the total energy (see the gas-phase "
"chemical potential in the `GaN surface phase diagram calculation example "
"<https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/gan_surface/phase_diagram.html>`__\\ )."

#: ../../thermo/gibbs_energy.rst:135
msgid ""
"同じ定義を電子に使ったものが、フェルミ–ディラック分布に現れる :ref:`電子の化学ポテンシャル<fermi-dirac-"
"distribution>`\\ である。2つの物質を接触させて電子が行き来できるとき、 :eq:`thermo-phase-"
"equilibrium`\\ と同じ理由で、平衡では両者のフェルミ準位がそろう。 "
"ただし、そろうのは静電ポテンシャルによるエネルギーを含め、共通のエネルギー基準（例えば真空準位）で測った "
"電子の化学ポテンシャル（電気化学ポテンシャル）である。物質ごとに価電子帯上端などから測った値はそろわない。"
msgstr ""
"Applying the same definition to electrons gives the :ref:`electron "
"chemical potential <fermi-dirac-distribution>`\\  that appears in the "
"Fermi–Dirac distribution. When two materials come into contact and "
"electrons can move between them, their Fermi levels align at equilibrium "
"for the same reason as in Equation :eq:`thermo-phase-equilibrium`\\ . The"
" quantities that align are the electron chemical potentials "
"(electrochemical potentials), including the energy due to the "
"electrostatic potential and measured relative to a common energy "
"reference, such as the vacuum level. Values measured relative to a "
"separate reference in each material, such as its valence band maximum, do"
" not align."

